ing on  right now and so we haven't just started  now but we've done several different  pilots to validate this approach and  this technology we've done a number of  pilot programs with the louisiana  biomedical research network kind of  hosted at the louisiana state university  with work with  georgetown university where we've  worked with the systems medicine program  where they kind of talk about the  clinical applications of bioinformatics  and we've worked with international  universities like the amity university  in  india where they have a number of  programs in biotechnology that really  need the bioinformatics training not as  a core subject but really as a subject  that could be implemented as a part of  the standard biotechnology  training and so in today's webinar in  today's sessions and tomorrow sessions  we will hear from a lot of these  programs about lessons learned you know  how does this work well uh in in terms  of where is this going where is the need  in the future for this kind of a domain  and also how can we prepare the students  not only to know what they need to know  today but also what kinds of skills they  will need in the next five to ten years  when they will become the leaders  of bioinformatics and so um we have a  lot of interesting participating  organizations that we will hear from  today that we already heard from some of  them up until now and of course we are  looking forward to today's sessions and  also tomorrow to hear about not only  what you can learn from some of the  training that we provide but also to get  a degree  in this area in this field  so  to summarize onyx logic is a program  that is designed to enable independent  research guided by mentors and peer  example and we are excited to see that  we have over 10 000 students learning in  different programs that we have  and we expect this number to continue to  grow as the need for bioinformatics is  expanding  we  see a need to kind of develop this  growing commu